Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 09:55:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: dt-bindings: stm32-sai: add power-domains property

STM32 SAI may be in a power domain. Allow power domains on SAI subnodes.

Change-Id: Ie798415eaede67ed260052b0f1f396277512535f
Signed-off-by: Olivier Moysan <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/567646
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/st,stm32-sai.yaml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/st,stm32-sai.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/st,stm32-sai.yaml
index 551edf39e766..7b1e4cb0b7e3 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/st,stm32-sai.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/st,stm32-sai.yaml
@@ -129,6 +129,9 @@ patternProperties:
         description: Configure the SAI device as master clock provider.
         const: 0
 
+      power-domains:
+        maxItems: 1
+
       port:
         $ref: audio-graph-port.yaml#
         unevaluatedProperties: false
